course: dictionary
lesson: 9032
title: Slant: a slope or a point of view
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A slant is a line or surface that slopes, not straight up or flat. To slant means to lean or slope. «Sunlight that falls at a slant spreads over more ground, so it warms each piece of ground less.» Here slant means the light comes in sideways, not straight down.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Spreads over more ground» and «warms each piece of ground less» show that the light is coming in at a slope. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Sunlight that falls at a sloping angle spreads over more ground» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Slant has a second meaning. It can be a particular way of seeing or telling something, sometimes unfairly. «A news story with a slant favours one side.» Ask yourself: does the story show both sides fairly, or does it lean one way?
fact: A slant is a line or surface that slopes, not straight up or flat.
fact: To slant means to lean or slope.
fact: A slant can also be a particular way of seeing or telling something, sometimes unfairly.
fact: «The polar zones are cold all year because the Sun's rays strike them at a low slant.»
fact: Useful phrases: «at a slant», «slanted writing», «a new slant on».
exercise: «The polar zones are cold all year because the Sun's rays strike them at a low slant.» What does at a slant mean here? | Very fast | Under the water | Straight down from above | *Sloping, not straight down
exercise: «A news story with a slant favours one side.» What does slant mean here? | *A way of telling a story that favours one side | A kind of sand on a beach | A straight line drawn with a ruler | A pen that writes very fast
exercise: In maths, a slanted line is also called a diagonal or an oblique line. What is another name for a slanted line? | Circular | Vertical | *Diagonal | Horizontal
test: In handwriting, letters may slant to the right. What does slant mean in «slanted writing»? | Read aloud to the class | *Leaning or sloping | Very neat and straight | Written in gold ink
test: Which sentence uses slant to mean a way of seeing or telling something? | «Letters may slant to the right in handwriting.» | *«A news story with a slant favours one side.» | «Sunlight that falls at a slant spreads over more ground.» | «Waves come in at a slant onto the beach.»
exam: Ayo reads, «The news story has a slant.» What should Ayo do before believing it? | Ignore it, because slant only means a line on paper | *Check whether the story shows both sides fairly | Read it upside down to see the real meaning | Trust it completely, because a slant is always true
